{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795429546,"nonce":"YIuQjsLtqhuXoW3EPeOnCBJDKQA=","title":"Python: type(x).__name__ of a boxed array is list","message":"A boxed array reports the type name list, where CPython says array. def f(x): return type(x).__name__, called as f(array('d', [1.0])), prints list; so does [type(v).__name__ for v in [array('i', [1]), [1]]]. A value of known type is right (e054c15e). isinstance on a boxed array is right too, because it tests the array kind range. The dynamic name comes from zb_any_type, whose TypeNames policy has no array entry and whose last arm returns the list name for every boxed list kind. Fix: a name for kinds at or above ARRAY_KIND_BASE in zb_any_type, with an empty or absent entry in the Lua policy. Repro: crates/zyntax_python/conformance/array, add a case printing the dynamic names.","files":null}]}